******************************************************************
*******************************************************************
I).   COP8 MOLE PERSONALITY BOARD SCRAMBLER AND JUMPER OPTIONS
*******************************************************************
TO CONNECT A TARGET SYSTEM TO THE REC-2 BOARD IT IS NECESSARY
TO USE THE MOLE COP888 SCRAMBLER BOARD, EXCEPT WHEN EMULATING COP888CF.

*******************************************************************
PB1A-BOARD(COP880/840/820)

 -44 PIN PLCC
  REMOVE ALL JUMPERS (W1-W6) ON THE SCRAMBLER BOARD

 -40 PIN DIP
  CONNECT PINS 1 AND 2 OF W3 AND PINS 1 AND 2 OF W4 ON THE S. BOARD

 -28 PIN DIP
  CONNECT PINS 2 AND 3 OF W5 AND PINS 2 AND 3 OF W6 ON THE S. BOARD

 -24/20 PIN DIP
  USE A SECOND SMALL 24/20 SCRAMBLER TO BE CONNECTED ON TOP OF THE
  INSTALLED SCRAMBLE BOARD. CONNECT PINS 2 AND 3 OF W5 AND
  PIN 2 AND 3 of W6.

*******************************************************************
PB2-BOARD(COP888CF/888CG/EG/888CL)

 -COP88XCF
  SCRAMBLER BOARD IS NOT USED

 -COP88XCG/EG

  44 PIN PLCC
  REMOVE ALL JUMPERS(W1-W6) ON THE SCRAMBLER BOARD

  40 PIN DIP
  CONNECT PINS 1 AND 2 OF W3 AND PINS 1 AND 2 OF W4

  28 PIN DIP/PLCC
  CONNECT PINS 2 AND 3 OF W5 AND PIN 2 AND 3 OF W6

 -COP88XCL

  44 PIN PLCC
  REMOVE ALL JUMPERS (W1-W6) ON THE SCRAMBLER BOARD

  40 PIN DIP
  CONNECT PINS 1 AND 2 OF W1, PIN 1 AND 2 OF W2, PINS 2 AND 3 OF W3 AND
  PIN 2 AND 3 OF W4

  28 PIN DIP/PLCC
  CONNECT PINS 1 AND 2 OF W1, PIN 1 AND 2 OF W2, PIN 1 AND 2 OF W5 AND
  PIN 1 AND 2 OF W6

******************************************************************

*******************************************************************
II).PROGRAMMABLE CLOCK GENERATOR (PCG) FOR MOLE DEVELOPMENT SYSTEM.
*******************************************************************
THE PCG-BOARD AS FAR AS POSSIBLE CAN BE USED TO RUN PROGRAMMS AT
DIFFERENT SPEEDS. TO AVOID DISPLAY PROBLEMS IT IS NECESSARY TO DO SOME
HARDWARE MODIFICATIONS.
IF PROBLEMS OCCUR PLEASE CHECK THE FOLLOWING.
- PIN 19/D0 (COP8720)MUST BE CONNECTED TO PIN 23 (MM5450).
- MAKE SURE THAT PIN 23 (MM5450) IS NOT CONNECTED TO GND.

******************************************************************

******************************************************************

III). MODIFICATION MOLE PB1 TO PB1A (Run DBCOP)

******************************************************************
DBCOP doesnt run with PB1 board in the normal configuration as
shipped.
TO RUN DBCOP WITH THE OLD PB1-BOARD IT IS NECESSARY TO DO SOME
MODIFICATIONS:

- PERSONALLITY-BOARD PB1

  HARDWARE-MODIFICATION:
  CUT THE TRACE FROM U59 PIN 5 TO U89 PIN 2.
  ADD A WIRE FROM U59 PIN 5 TO U59 PIN 11.
  ADD A WIRE FROM U59 PIN 10 TO U59 PIN 13.
  ADD A WIRE FROM U59 PIN 12 TO U89 PIN 2.

- REC1-BOARD(COP820/840)
  REPLACE THE RESIDENT FIRMWARE WITH THE LATEST FIRMWARE REVISION.
  FIRMWARE: COP880/REV.4.50 CHECKSUM 5D64
  MOLE-DEVICE: COP840

- REC2-BOARD(COP820/840/880)
  REPLACE THE RESIDENT FIRMWARE WITH THE LATEST FIRMWARE REVISION.
  FIRMWARE: COP880/REV.4.50 CHECKSUM 5D64
  MOLE-DEVICE: COP880 (44PIN)
******************************************************************

******************************************************************
IV).       RC-CLOCK COP800
******************************************************************
There are some mistakes in the COP8 Char.data report with regard to
RC clock frequencies given.
The correct RC CKI-freq. for all COP800 members are as follow:

TA=25C
  R(KOhm)      C(pF)      CKI(MHz)      Instr.Cycle(us)      Conditions
  3.3           82        2.8-2.2       3.6-4.5              VCC=5V
  5.6          100        1.5-1.1       6.7-9                VCC=5V
  6.8          100        1.1-0.8       9-12.5               VCC=5V

Some Datasheets e.g. COP820CJ include the wrong data for the RC-Oscill. freg.
also.
We will probaly come up with an addendum to the Char.report with correct values.
We will keep you informed.
******************************************************************

