VII).     U A R T  SYNCHRONOUS mode in COP888CG:

The main purpose of SYNCHRONOUS mode in our UART's (COP8 and HPC) is to
increase the data rate. SYNCHRONOUS mode is entered in COP888CG by sett-
int ENUI.SSEL (bit4). In addition, one must also select EXTERNAL CLOCK
by setting ENUI.XRCLK(bit3) and ENUI.XTCLK (bit2).  This is  necessary
even if shift clock is generated internally.
In SYNCHRONOUS MODE the state of the UART in the COP888CG is as follows:

1.) If you selected a baud rate of - say - 9600 for asynchronous mode,
    then the shift clock is now in synchronous mode 76800 Hz, yielding
    a period of 13 usec. This frequency is used for the internal shift-
    registers and is made available at CKX (if PORTL bit1 is configured
    as output - of course). The synchronous baud rate of 76800 results
    from removing the DIV16 prescalers (in asynchronous mode) and re-
    placing them by a DIV2 in synchronous mode: 9600 * 16 / 2 = 76800.
2.) The TDX output is '1' between frames.
3.) The number of data bits, stop bits and parity type must still be se-
    lected exactly as in normal asynchronous mode.
4.) The receiver still expects a high-to-low transition as START bit.
5.) Data is still shifted LSB first.


The following initialisation illustrates how to use the COP888CG UART in
synchronous mode (10 Mhz crystal and COP888CG delivers the UART clock):


        ...
        SBIT    2,PORTLD        ;B2(TDX)=1. (TO AVOID UNDESIRED START-BIT)
        SBIT    2,PORTLC        ;B2(TDX) is O/P.
        SBIT    1,PORTLC        ;B1(CKX) is O/P.
        RBIT    3,PORTLC        ;B3(RDX) is I/P (not needed after RESET).
        LD      PSR,    #0xC8   ;PRESCALE FACTOR 13.
        LD      BAUD,   #0x04   ;N-1. (9600 BAUD OR 104 USEC PER BIT IN
                                ;UART MODE and
                                ;9600*8=76800 BAUD OR 13 USEC PER BIT
                                ;IN USART MODE).
        LD      ENU,    #0x00   ;PAR_DIS,ODD,8DTA (not needed after RESET).
        LD      ENUR,   #0x00   ;ATTN_DIS (not needed after RESET).
        LD      ENUI,   #0x3C   ;1STP,ETDX,SSEL,CLK_EXT,INTR'S_DIS.
                                ;MUST be external clock in SYNCHR. mode!
                                ;Otherwise no clock at PORTL bit1.
        ...

***********************************************************************

